@startuml scheduled_run_sequence
' Baseline: Claude scheduled-deployments, checked 2026-09-29, Beta.
' Source: modules/cron/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/cron/engine/CronEngine.java executeAndReschedule.
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/RuntimeExecutionPersistenceService.java acceptMessage.
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventOutput.java persistenceOnly.
' Java baseline: 553dcd5e2ff682f9684810a043b442b37a02e54a.
' Design reason: durable occurrence and atomic acceptance, guarded against deletion, precede external work.
' Architecture change: scheduled acceptance and persistent Cron sessions are Pending implementation.
' Product constraints: no catch-up, skip when busy, no replay after failure or lost ownership.
' Product constraints: Mate supplies trusted definitions and credentials; no interactive scheduled work.
title Daily alarm summary - new session (Pending implementation)
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
participant Scheduler
participant Host
database Store
participant Runtime
participant AgentLoop
Scheduler -> Store : Claim current occurrence and task slot\nInsert Run, advance future cursor; commit
Store --> Scheduler : Run identity and claim epoch
Scheduler -> Host : Prepare Agent snapshot\nResolve Mate definitions, grant and credential references
Host --> Scheduler : Prepared run or rejection
alt Preparation rejected
  Scheduler -> Store : Record failure only for existing task / Run\nRelease own slot; no retry
  Store --> Scheduler : Durable failure or deletion preserved
else Preparation ready
  Scheduler -> Runtime : Accept Run with prepared snapshot
  Runtime -> Store : Require existing, non-deleted task\nRecheck state, time, claim and capacity\nCreate Session, message, root execution\nand Run link in one transaction
  Store --> Runtime : Committed acceptance
  Runtime --> Scheduler : Accepted identity (not completion)
  Runtime -> Store : CAS READY to STARTING for live owner
  Store --> Runtime : Single start grant
  Runtime ->> AgentLoop : Start through shared Session factory
  note right of AgentLoop
    Target -> arguments -> permission
    -> credentials -> business execution -> result.
    ASK ends this root through the Host.
    No automatic approval or durable wait.
  end note
  AgentLoop -> Runtime : Content and actual root outcome
  Runtime -> Store : Persist events and root terminal state
  Store --> Runtime : Durable outcome
  Scheduler -> Store : Reconcile fixed root execution\nUpdate existing task / Run only; release own slot
  Store --> Scheduler : Existing history updated or cleanup only
end
note over Scheduler, Runtime
  Rejection records failure only while task / Run exist.
  Duplicate acceptance returns the existing link only.
  Pause after acceptance does not cancel the Run.
  Deletion does not cancel an already accepted Session.
  Deletion removes Schedule and Run; Session remains independent.
  Late completion never recreates deleted Schedule or Run.
  Internal coordination remains until safe cleanup.
  Lost owner requires reconciliation, not replay.
  No catch-up after restart; busy occurrences are skipped.
  Unknown outcomes remain unknown and keep the task busy.
end note
@enduml

@startuml scheduled_task_architecture
' Baseline: Claude Deployment / Run / Session and run/pause/unpause, checked 2026-10-05, Beta.
' Source: modules/cron/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/cron/CronService.java createJob and triggerJob.
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/tool/cron/ManagedCronSessionRunner.java execute.
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeExecutionCoordinator.java start and commitTerminal.
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/session/AgentSessionFactory.java create.
' Java baseline: 553dcd5e2ff682f9684810a043b442b37a02e54a.
' Design reason: preserve API, service, policy, adapter, runtime and durable boundaries.
' Product constraint: every Run creates a new Session using the bound Agent definition.
' Architecture change: Cron merges into coding-agent-cli; no independent cron artifact.
' Source: pom.xml modules; scripts/sync-campusclaw.sh MODULES.
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/RuntimeSessionEngineRegistry.java createSession.
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/tool/cron/AgentScopedCronToolFactory.java create.
' Design reason: thin admission has no dependency on the dispatcher or execution registry.
' Architecture change: one acceptance path; no existing-session target strategy.
' Architecture change: every P node and every connector is Pending implementation.
title Scheduled tasks - global target
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 55
hide empty members
class "Calling service" as Caller <<External>>
class "ScheduleController" as Api <<API / P>>
class "CronToolAdapter" as Tool <<Adapter / P>>
class "ScheduleApplication\nService" as App <<Management / P>>
class "ScheduleDispatcher" as Dispatch <<Service / P>>
interface "ScheduleAuthorization\nPort" as Auth <<Port / P>>
interface "ScheduleCredential\nPort" as Credential <<Port / P>>
class "MateSchedule\nAdapter" as MateAdapter <<Adapter / P>>
class "Mate service" as Mate <<External>>
interface "ScheduleBinding\nResolver" as Binding <<Read-only port / P>>
class "ScheduleTime\nPolicy" as Time <<Policy / P>>
class "ScheduleRun\nPreparation" as Prepare <<Service / P>>
class "PreparedSchedule\nRunDTO" as Snapshot <<Immutable / P>>
interface "ScheduleRepository" as Repo <<Port / P>>
class "MyBatisSchedule\nRepository" as RepoImpl <<Adapter / P>>
interface "ScheduleMapper" as Mapper <<DTO boundary / P>>
class "GaussDB\nSchedule / Run / Dispatch state\nSession / Execution" as Db <<Durable authority>>
class "ScheduledRunAcceptance\nService" as Accept <<Service / P>>
class "Runtime session and\nexecution persistence" as Persist <<Existing>>
class "RuntimeExecution\nCoordinator" as Coordinator <<Existing>>
class "AgentSession\nFactory" as Factory <<Existing>>
class "ManagedAgentSession" as Session <<Per execution>>
class "Host hooks +\nToolExecutionPipeline" as Pipeline <<Per execution>>
Caller -down-> Api : Claw VO
Api -down-> App : VO boundary
App -down-> Prepare : manual
App -[norank]-> Accept : manual admit
Tool -down-> App : bound scope
App -down[hidden]-> Dispatch
Binding -down[hidden]-> Auth
Auth -down[hidden]-> Credential
App -left-> Time : validate / preview
App -right-> Repo : lock latest row\nwrite DTO
App -[norank]-> Auth
App -left-> Binding : validate references
Dispatch -down-> Accept : accept run
Dispatch -left-> Prepare : automatic
Dispatch -[norank]-> Time
Dispatch -[norank]-> Repo
Prepare -left-> Auth : authorize
Pipeline -left-> Credential : resolve after permission
Prepare -down-> Snapshot
MateAdapter .right.|> Auth
MateAdapter .right.|> Binding
MateAdapter .right.|> Credential
MateAdapter -down-> Mate : definitions / grants\nand credentials
Accept -left-> Snapshot : fixed input
Accept -[norank]-> Repo
Repo <|.. RepoImpl
RepoImpl -down-> Mapper
Mapper -down-> Db
Accept -down-> Persist : create / accept
Persist -right-> Db : same transaction
Dispatch -down-> Coordinator : start once\nafter commit
Coordinator -right-> Persist : events / terminal
Coordinator -down-> Factory
Factory -down-> "0..*" Session : creates
Session *-down-> "1" Pipeline
legend bottom
  P = Pending implementation; all new connectors are pending.
  Existing services need scheduled-entry integration.
  Services are singletons; snapshots and sessions are per Run.
  All Claw target services live in coding-agent-cli.
  HTTP: runtimeapi; scheduling: schedule; tool adapter: tool.cron.
  Mate APIs supply trusted bindings, authorization and credentials.
  Configuration handlers never call prepare or start a Session.
  A rule registers automatic work; no rule only saves.
  Each Run creates a Session, not an Agent definition.
  No catch-up or execution replay; busy occurrences are skipped.
  ASK ends the root; no durable interaction wait.
  Unknown execution is reconciled, never reported as a known failure.
  Run + message + execution commit before model or tool I/O.
  Schedule deletion removes Run and public run history.
  Deletion does not cancel accepted Sessions.
  Session deletion keeps the original Run admission receipt.
  No separate cron module or second legacy scheduler.
  Thin admission never depends on Dispatcher or Runtime Registry.
  Internal in-flight coordination remains only until safe cleanup.
endlegend
@enduml

@startuml schedule_configuration_save
' Target: Pending implementation; Claw configuration request, no in-request execution.
' Evidence: pi-mono-java 553dcd5e2ff682f9684810a043b442b37a02e54a
' modules/cron/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/cron/CronService.java createJob
' modules/cron/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/cron/store/CronStore.java saveUnsafe
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtime/AgentRuntimeManager.java prepare
' Design reason: durable independent creation and read-only Mate binding checks.
' Product constraint: text-only initial message; credentials remain references at rest.
title Claw schedule configuration - Pending implementation
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
hide footbox
actor Caller
participant Schedule
participant Mate
database Store
Caller -> Schedule : Create configuration
Schedule -> Schedule : Authenticate; authorize scope\nValidate request shape
Schedule -> Mate : Read trusted Agent and credential bindings\nand current management grant
Mate --> Schedule : Binding or typed rejection
Schedule -> Schedule : Validate complete configuration and rule
break Binding or rule rejected
  Schedule --> Caller : Safe typed error; no write
end
Schedule -> Store : Insert active configuration with new ID\nCommit one transaction
Store --> Schedule : Committed resource or rollback
Schedule --> Caller : 201 resource + Location\nor safe typed failure
note over Caller, Store
  Text-only initial message; no attachment acceptance.
  No Session, model, tool, or directory publication in this request.
  Store credential references only; resolve secrets at execution.
  A rule registers automatic work; no rule only saves.
  Each successful create allocates a new configuration ID.
  Lost response: inspect saved resources before another write.
end note
@enduml

